  "caveats": [
    "U(1)-framing ladder verdict: writhe(T(2,n)) = n is nonzero and STRICTLY INCREASING across the lepton tower (3,5,7,9), so the framing factor q^{n.c} is a per-lepton LADDER (monotone in generation), NOT a constant. But the lepton ELECTRIC CHARGE is the SAME (-1) for e, mu, tau -- a constant. So writhe -> electric charge is a CATEGORY MISMATCH (monotone ladder vs constant); the framing U(1) does NOT reproduce electric charge. The framing ladder DOES track generation number (n=2k+1 for generation k), which is the cyclic-symmetry index Z_n, NOT a gauge charge. No coupling c is tuned (c=1 set); writhe -> Y remains undefined, consistent with the inter-nucleon linked-channel audit (misses PDG split by ~305x at c=1).",
